Begin GEA_TSP

1. INPUT:
      - List of cities
      - Distance matrix between every pair of cities

2. SET parameters:
      POP_SIZE
      MUTATION_RATE
      GENERATIONS

3. CREATE initial population:
      For i = 1 to POP_SIZE
            route = random permutation of cities
            add route to population

4. DEFINE fitness function:
      fitness(route) = 1 / total_distance(route)

5. For generation = 1 to GENERATIONS:

         a. Evaluate population fitness
             Sort population by total_distance ascending

         b. Selection:
             selected_parents = best 50% of population

         c. Crossover + Mutation:
             new_population = empty
             While size(new_population) < POP_SIZE
                   parent1, parent2 = randomly select two from selected_parents
                   child = Order_Crossover(parent1, parent2)
                   child = Mutate(child, MUTATION_RATE)
                   add child to new_population

         d. Replace population = new_population

         e. Track best_route so far based on minimum distance

6. OUTPUT best_route and best_distance

End GEA_TSP
